  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, PCA, single-profile at ~48.5% acc), the highest-uncertainty question is whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the simplest image-only baseline and directly answers this. If image-only accuracy is competitive or strong, the large multimodal subspace (configs 16-51) becomes a promising exploitation target for the remaining 7 experiments. If it is weak, we can deprioritize multimodal configs and focus on RNA encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt) or multiprofile aggregation. This is a clean single-variable shift (modality) from the baseline, keeping profile setting and complexity level comparable, so the result isolates the value of visual information. Under a 10-experiment budget, resolving the modality question early is the most information-dense use of experiment 2."
}

